{{!--
  Overrides `partials/header-content.hbs` from Antora's default UI
  bundle, which ships a demo navbar: Home, a Products dropdown with
  Product A/B/C, a Services dropdown with Service A/B/C, and a Download
  button. Every one of them is `href="#"` - placeholders for a project
  that has products to sell, which this does not.

  Supplied through `ui.supplemental_files` rather than by forking the
  bundle or stripping the markup afterwards, which is the mechanism
  Antora provides for exactly this: one file replaces one file, and the
  rest of the UI keeps updating with the bundle.

  What is left is the site title, linking home. The burger button goes
  with the menu it toggled - with nothing to expand it is a control
  that does nothing, and on a narrow screen it would still be drawn.
--}}
<header class="header">
  <nav class="navbar">
    <div class="navbar-brand">
      <a class="navbar-item" href="{{{or site.url siteRootPath}}}">{{site.title}}</a>
    </div>
  </nav>
</header>
